# Vendored third-party binaries — sha256 manifest
#
# 🔴 `hash_source` IS A FIELD ON EVERY ROW, NOT A COMMENT, AND IT IS THE POINT OF THIS FILE.
# It records where each expected hash was computed from: the gradle CACHE — the bytes every
# tested APK, every device smoke and the green beta gate were built from — independently
# cross-checked against a fresh jitpack fetch on 2026-08-17 (27/27 files identical).
#
# ⚠️ NEVER regenerate these hashes FROM third_party/m2/. A hash whose expected value is derived
#    from the file it checks does not fail — it passes forever, and the check degenerates into a
#    file proving it matches itself. To re-verify: re-fetch upstream and diff, or restore from a
#    cache whose provenance you can state. A regenerator that repoints hash_source at the
#    vendored tree is FALSIFYING this field, not updating it.
#
# .pom AND .module are attested too, not just the .aar: Gradle PREFERS Gradle Module Metadata
# (.module) over the POM, and vendoring without it silently changed the resolved graph the first
# time this was attempted (kotlin-stdlib-jdk7/jdk8 dropped out of both configurations). The
# metadata is part of what determines the shipped classpath, so it is part of what is attested.
#
# Columns: coordinates | version | licence | licence_file | file | sha256 | hash_source

